architecture program-fabric
  canonical_name ProgramFabric
  family capability
  domain Programs / Institutional capability configuration
  layer configuration
  semantic_question How does a subject start running a generalized capability without the estate growing another product, another page tree, or another store?
  purpose The binding layer that records a subject preparing or using a program and names the existing owners that should participate: its world and slots, SourceFrontier, work and evidence graphs, and Finance. It owns configuration, not those owners' material, work or money. Shared authenticated WebAddress chrome presents private preparation, maintained configuration and exact continuations to the existing work owners.
  maturity implemented
  node_types ProgramTemplate
  node_types ProgramInstance
  node_types ProgramRequirement
  node_types FundingWorkPackage
  node_types ProgramBinding
  edge_types instantiates
  edge_types binds_into
  edge_types obliges
  edge_types funds_scope
  internal_calculus a template declares the subject kinds, slots, capability families and owners a program of that kind needs; it is not an instance and names a funding stream only as the kind of stream such work is usually paid by
  internal_calculus an instance exists only when a real subject uses the program, and adds its slots after whatever that subject's world already publishes, so attaching one never reorders the subject's own composition
  internal_calculus a program role is lowered by an application only where an application genuinely lowers that material; the rest are published as declared slots that no surface can fill yet, which the machine projection states and the page omits
  internal_calculus a capability family becomes an open ProgramRequirement rather than a capability_program, because this estate's capability_program is an action contract carrying an authority requirement and a failure projection, and writing one without those would be maturity laundering
  internal_calculus several funding streams may support one real effort; each is a distinct work package whose scope and cost codes must not overlap another on the same instance, which is what lets one effort funded three ways be told apart from one cost claimed three times
  invariant an instance owns no material, no work, no evidence and no money; every one of those stays with the owner that already holds it
  invariant a program never requires a page; a dedicated surface exists only when an institution chooses to expose one
  invariant a work package's scope stays distinct from every other package on the same instance
  forbidden_inference a template -> a program anyone is running, an award, an application for one, or any relationship with the funder it names
  forbidden_inference an instance -> authority to act on anyone's behalf, a funded award, or an entitlement held by the owning subject
  forbidden_inference a funding work package -> money awarded, applied for, billed, paid, booked, or authorized to spend
  forbidden_inference an open requirement -> an obligation met, or authority to meet it
  forbidden_inference a declared slot with no lowering application -> a feature that exists, or one that failed
