  witness 2026-09-19 fifty generalized program templates loaded across nine archetypes, and four of them compiled onto one real subject produced 4 instances, 27 slots, 27 program bindings, 45 open requirements and 12 funding work packages without creating a single application, page or route
  witness 2026-09-19 of the 27 compiled slots, 8 were lowered by an application this estate actually has and 19 were published as declared slots no surface can fill; the lowered ones rendered the estate's own empty characters rather than blank sections, and nick.aurekai.life composed unchanged at 60 KB
  internal_calculus a program's stated needs are the discovery query: the demand recorded in its collection is asked of SourceFrontier through the ordinary admission chain -- listed, imported under this instance's own label, qualified, and for the pages that answered, qualified again on the feeds those pages declare -- and only what answered is named in the collection
  source_path scripts/resolve_program_sources.mjs
  source_path scripts/resolve_program_sources.py.archive
  source_path scripts/tests/resolve_program_sources_test.mjs
  invariant only a source admitted by SourceFrontier under this instance's label can enter its collection; a missing published collection is refused rather than marking the source-intake requirement met without an owner
  witness scripts/tests/resolve_program_sources_test.mjs proves a dry run makes no provider call, a missing instance is refused, and a listed candidate reaches the program collection and closes source-intake only after qualification and admitted SourceFrontier state
  source_path scripts/bootstrap_funding_frontier.py.archive
  source_path scripts/bootstrap_funding_frontier.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/bootstrap-funding-frontier.test.mjs
  witness 2026-09-19 the permit program's eight stated needs resolved through the whole chain: 60 addresses listed, 59 asked, 9 publisher-declared feeds found, 3 admitted, and those 3 named in that program's own collection; nothing shortened the chain and the 56 that did not answer are absent rather than assumed
  source_lineage the earlier Exa-first resolver returned three loosely related sources from sixty listed addresses; that discovery-first path and its hardcoded archetype search dictionary have been replaced by shared owner resolution
  known_gap a resolved source is named in the collection before anything has read it; items appear only after the standing pass reheats it, so a program collection can name sources whose material is not yet in the archive
  known_gap resolution binds candidate references and rechecks published source membership, not arbitrary capability fulfillment or finance acceptance; exact execution and acceptance remain with those owners
  known_gap the fifty templates arrived as an external pack; their archetypes and slot vocabularies are that pack's, not this estate's measured vocabulary, and only the eight roles this estate can lower have been reconciled with its applications
  known_gap the native program compiler passed fixture parity against the retired Python writer and rolls back a failed compile, but the fifty-template live estate has not been replayed through this cutover
  source_path scripts/recurring-commerce-load.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/recurring-commerce-native.test.mjs
  witness 2026-10-03 scripts/tests/recurring-commerce-native.test.mjs, run as a script against a temporary native CMS: ten reference provider profiles as external_resource and thirty-six recurring-commerce templates across eight contract shapes compiled into 36 instances, 144 slots, 144 application bindings and 180 open requirements, with billing_connected false
  witness 2026-10-03 the local estate's program_template holds 86 rows: the fifty earlier templates and these thirty-six (recurring_service 8, discovery_box 7, replenishment 6, hybrid 6, access_pass 4, finite_gift 3, wardrobe_keep_all 1, try_before_buy 1); a dry run of the loader reports nothing to create
  forbidden_inference a reference provider profile -> a merchant account, a partnership, current price or stock, or a checkout connection with that provider
  forbidden_inference a recurring-commerce template -> a subscription anyone holds, a charge, a reservation or a delivery
  source_path scripts/recurring-commerce/draft.mjs
  source_path scripts/recurring-commerce/catalog.json
  witness scripts/tests/recurring-commerce-draft.test.mjs holds the draft compiler lifted from the delivered studio to what it was said to do: a monthly anchor on the 31st lands on each month's last day and returns to the 31st; a styling fee already paid is credited against what is kept and returning everything leaves the fee; replenishment is proposed only from a stated observation no more than seven days old and never grants a charge; selection rejects repeats, excluded ingredients, heat over the ceiling and unverified stock, and treats missing ingredients as unverified; a finite gift cannot auto-renew and is counted once; a budget preview leaves try-on, replenishment and mixed programs unpriced; the catalogue maps to ten profiles and thirty-six templates in eight shapes with every bundle naming real templates
  forbidden_inference a compiled draft or a budget preview -> a merchant connection, consent, an invoice, a payment, a stock reservation, a shipment or an active renewal
  known_gap the thirty-six recurring-commerce templates and ten provider profiles arrived as an external pack, like the fifty before them. The draft compiler and catalogue are now in this checkout and tested; the studio page itself is not, because a standalone page is not how this estate exposes authoring, and the installed browser workbench now calls the canonical recurring compiler. The live store's rows carry the loader's shorter descriptions rather than the catalogue's, the native witness is a script bun test does not collect, and no instance of any of them runs on a real subject

