  native_format MessagePack
  internal_calculus the shared /programs frontdoor reads published templates and private prepared instances through the native ProgramFabric owner; /apps/_programs carries bounded versioned MessagePack for catalogue, preparation, configuration changes, receipts and declared source work instead of a parallel browser registry
  internal_calculus WebAddress resolves the live actor, selected subject and scope from native account and membership admission on every request; preparation, configuration changes and source mutations additionally require current write access and an expected binding that still equals that admitted destination
  internal_calculus a new account preparation derives its site identity from the fixed namespace, subject and scope; it compiles through the same ProgramFabric transaction and retains draft instances, slots, bindings, source collections, open requirements and distinct funding work packages
  internal_calculus review binds the whole template row, compiler policy and admitted actor/subject/scope; prepare rechecks that digest inside the same immediate transaction that compiles the instance, records its owner receipt and checks the bounded response
  invariant the browser cannot choose an actor, owner subject, site identity, namespace, database or native program-owner executable; the deployment configures native paths and the edge supplies current admitted identity
  invariant private readback filters every instance by namespace and owner_subject before reading its requirements, bindings or funding work packages; a template catalogue cannot widen that ownership
  invariant a retained preparation reopens its deterministic instance without recompiling accepted requirements, authored funding scopes or logical timestamps; changed templates and preexisting unreceipted instances or child identities are refused rather than adopted
  invariant an observed account change or current access refusal clears prior private browser projections; late replies cannot repopulate the previous destination, and an unconfirmed write keeps the exact instance address for readback before any new preparation
  invariant private preparation does not publish or demote existing public records and cannot mark a requirement met, select provider credentials or execute an external action
  invariant installed editor links name current admitted workspace bindings; attached work names a native-verified exact key, revision, release and body digest with a compatible saved-record view, and the record body remains with its existing editor
  witness scripts/tests/program-workspace-owner.test.mjs checks exact review, private compilation, account and namespace isolation, stale bindings, replay preservation, unreceipted and orphan identity refusal, transaction rollback and bounded MessagePack transport
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/program_workspace.test.mjs exercises the real C gateway with controlled authority and subprocess replies, including current read/write admission, method and origin checks, owner argument binding and malformed native packet refusal
  witness integrations/browser/tests/program-workspace.browser.test.mjs uses the real owner, compiler and SQLite with fixture account admission and controlled AddressPlane results to check browser preparation, retained requirements, installed editor links, access revocation, stale account replies and repeated readback after a lost acknowledgement
  known_gap existing operator and person:nick instances have no implied authenticated account owner; this frontdoor prepares new admitted instances and cannot transfer or reinterpret those earlier records
  known_gap a declared facility, farm, municipality or other domain subject is not an account, institution or household; templates that do not admit one of the currently selected subject kinds require an explicit future target binding
  known_gap requirement deadlines and funding scope are editable configuration, and actual source research can run through SourceFrontier; evidence acceptance, partner or institution commitments, financial approval and Program-to-Model-Commons task attachment remain with their native owners or require a further explicit bridge
  known_gap fixtures verify configuration, saved-work continuation and source execution with controlled provider results; they do not attest current provider availability, a production research result or a delivered notification; managed deployment must freeze both Program owners, native CMS and AddressPlane readers, SourceFrontier protocol dependencies, browser components and configured canonical databases
  forbidden_inference a prepared account program or an installed editor link -> an activated institution, copied work record, trusted ownership of a legacy operator task, accepted requirement, partner agreement or external effect
  forbidden_inference a successful local program preparation -> public publication, submitted funding application, provider connection, paid model run or execution authority

