  internal_calculus the workspace composes maintained work, source research, funding and overview panels with shared searchable collections and inspectors; unsaved edits survive panel changes only in account-bound memory and are removed on account invalidation
  internal_calculus configuration saves compare the full admitted Program revision inside one immediate transaction, retain an exact request digest and outcome receipt, and expose a read-only receipt lookup after an interrupted acknowledgement
  internal_calculus editable requirement deadlines leave owner state and accepted evidence unchanged; funding scope and cost-code declarations reject normalized overlap with other packages in that same Program
  internal_calculus work attachments verify the current CMS install, subject, scope, record key, revision, release and body digest through the existing continuation owner, then verify retained saved-view material; the CMS continuation reader opens the database read-only so a Program transaction can hold its configuration lock
  internal_calculus local source refresh consumes the existing AddressPlane resolver and preserves draft lifecycle and accepted evidence; it does not run external discovery
  internal_calculus a source plan binds one actual Program collection and declared demand to a reviewed SourceFrontier request; ProgramFabric retains only the association and digests while WebWork retains the plan, provider reply, results, review decisions and exact text
  invariant source planning and start are separate actions; start reuses the native source-read admission, quotas, credentials, reviewed digest, revision and no-repeat-dispatch transition without changing any of those gates
  invariant no CMS configuration transaction spans a provider request; an interrupted association resolves through the same retained WebWork request and can never turn uncertainty into a new automatic dispatch
  invariant source status, retained results and configuration receipts require current read access; source planning, execution, result review and configuration edits require current write access and an exact expected actor, subject and scope
  invariant attached source jobs use the existing account-scoped Activity and Outputs projection and exact source-workbench continuation; research results, source-library material, source-collection admission and accepted requirement evidence remain distinct owner states
  witness scripts/tests/program-workspace-owner.test.mjs checks planning edits, full revision conflict, idempotent receipt recovery, cross-account refusal, funding overlap, native record verification and preservation of accepted state
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/program_continuation_test.c drives actual CMS plan, install, activate and workspace write commands before six continuation checks: a 2.5-second read under BEGIN IMMEDIATE, exact retained MessagePack record, same-account workspace contexts, unchanged schema and database/WAL bytes, cross-account refusal, and missing-database refusal without creation; tests/program_continuation_test.mk supports native and ASan/UBSan execution and honors BONFYRE_TEST_PROGRAM_CMS_BINARY for the frozen reader
  witness scripts/tests/program-source-work.test.mjs checks current Program ownership, exact collection/demand review, durable native plan association, uncertain acknowledgement recovery, source admission, no duplicate dispatch and retained result identity with controlled providers
  witness integrations/browser/tests/program-workspace.browser.test.mjs exercises actual saves and source continuation through native owners with account invalidation, scoped drafts, conflicts, exact saved-record reopening and interrupted acknowledgements
  witness scripts/release/tests/public_surface_rollout.test.mjs checks frozen native and browser dependency closure, canonical database configuration and exact asset readback
  forbidden_inference a planned deadline, saved funding scope, attached editor record or shortlisted source result -> accepted evidence, fulfilled capability, eligibility, partner consent, an award or spend authority
  forbidden_inference a source plan or retained association -> provider execution; only the native reviewed Start transition may initiate that request

  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/data/work-example-programs.jsonl
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/tools/install_work_examples.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/work_example_programs_test.sh
  internal_calculus a released WorkExample names one reusable program_template; /programs?context=C&template=T reads the admitted catalogue and private instances for C, opens the existing instance of T owned by C when one exists and otherwise shows the published template unreviewed; it never sends review, prepare or any write on arrival
  internal_calculus the template deep link is accepted only on the human /programs page, is exclusive with instance, matches the catalogue's template identity grammar (alphanumeric lead, at most 160 of [A-Za-z0-9._-]), survives sign-in and a workspace switch, and is refused on the /apps/_programs machine carrier
  internal_calculus the seven finished-work templates (shop layout and fixture buying, one catalogue from several shops, staffing a service queue, workbook assumption review, research to a migration plan, planning recurring selections, continuing a recording session) are installed create-only beside the examples; an existing template is never rewritten because prepared programs retain its reviewed digest
  invariant a template deep link selects nothing outside the current admitted destination: the instance it opens comes from that destination's owner-filtered readback, and another account reaching the same link sees only the published template
  invariant the material and organizations an example was built with stay in WorkExample.made_with as provenance; the reusable template a visitor starts names none of them
  witness integrations/browser/tests/program-workspace.browser.test.mjs "a template link opens the reviewed template unprepared, then only this account's prepared program" drives real Chrome against the real owner and compiler: the template opens with no review, prepare, change or source write; after preparation the same link reopens that instance; a second account sees only the template; an unknown template says it is not offered
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/profile_site_scope.test.mjs "released work stays with its bound account profile" runs the native binary: the profile CTA is /programs?context=self&template=..., /programs carries data-template and keeps it across the workspace switch and sign-in redirect, and malformed, duplicate, over-long, instance-combined and machine-carrier template links answer 400
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/work_example_programs_test.sh installs the shipped data into a fresh native CMS: every example binds a published person-startable template, reinstall leaves an owner-edited template unchanged, an example naming a missing or draft template is refused before it is written, the schema declares every data field and no unused terms field, and no made_with name appears in template text
  forbidden_inference a work example's template link or an opened template -> a prepared program, a reviewed preparation, the profile owner's records, or an endorsement by the material named in made_with
  known_gap the seven finished-work templates exist in source and in fixture databases only; the live CMS needs install_work_examples.sh run against it, and no live work_example row is bound to a profile site yet, so no public profile shows released work today
  known_gap the deep link's existing-instance choice is the first owner-filtered instance of that template; a destination holding several instances of one template (possible only through earlier operator compilation) opens the first, not a chooser

interaction program-fabric-projects-authenticated-preparation
  source program-fabric
  destination web-address-edge
  relation projects_private_preparation_into_shared_account_chrome
  preserves freshly admitted actor/subject/scope binding, selected destination, exact template and review digest, deterministic instance identity, private owner readback, retained requirement state and installed workspace identity
  drops caller-selected owner or namespace, legacy ownership inference, browser persistence of private account records, material duplication and any claim that a declared role has executed
  invalidates_on current session or membership admission, selected actor/subject/scope, whole template or compiler policy digest, current instance ownership or installed workspace binding changing
  forbidden_inference template review, saved preparation or continuation link -> owner acceptance, background execution, funding, model metering, provider consent or an external effect
  binding scripts/program-workspace-owner.mjs
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/program_workspace.h
  binding integrations/browser/program-workspace.mjs
  witness scripts/tests/program-workspace-owner.test.mjs
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/program_workspace.test.mjs
  witness integrations/browser/tests/program-workspace.browser.test.mjs

interaction program-fabric-projects-funding-prospect-frontier
  source program-fabric
  destination funding-prospect-frontier
  relation projects_published_institutional_pilot_editions_and_funding_work_packages_for_public_observation
  preserves published ProgramInstance identity, declared semantic slots, work-package boundary and declared funding rail
  drops activated public/member/operator material, partner relationship, programme eligibility, applicant identity evidence, application content, provider response tokens, award state, money and spend authority
  forbidden_inference a proposed public/member/operator pilot edition or a declared funding rail projected into public discovery -> activated material, partner relationship, submitted application, eligible applicant, award or spend authority
  invalidates_on published ProgramInstance, FundingWorkPackage, public observation receipt or query-vocabulary mapping changing
  witness scripts/tests/bootstrap-funding-frontier.test.mjs
  binding scripts/bootstrap_funding_frontier.py

